Rule 13 (If tensors are provided, at least one of them must have a non-zero number of dimensions)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) > 0
>>
Rule 14 (The size of a dimension must be greater than 0)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) > 0
>>
Rule 15 (The number of dimensions should be less than or equal to the maximum number of dimensions allowed for a tensor, which is a finite number)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) ≤ 6
>>
Rule 16 (If a tensor has a size of zero for a dimension, then resulting tensor also has that size of zero for that dimension)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= (∃i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) = 0) ∨ (∃i ∈ [0, ndim(v_2) - 1] : shape(v_2, i) = 0)
>>
Rule 17 (Either both tensors have the same number of dimensions or the smaller tensor has number of dimensions zero)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= (ndim(v_1) = ndim(v_2)) ∨ (ndim(v_1) = 0) ∨ (ndim(v_2) = 0)
